oot_or_none precedence: 'explicit > REBAR_ROOT > git toplevel of cwd, or None' (_config_resolvers.py:239-264)","The bare-resolver sites take only `tracker`: e.g. reads.py:238 `_sync_disabled(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(tracker)))`, freshness.py:80 `base = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(tracker))`","The guard docstring's assumption 'REBAR_ROOT covers the relocated deployment' (check_repo_root_from_tracker.py:47-48) is asserted, not proven for these call sites","The relocated topology is precisely 'store outside the code checkout' — the case where git-toplevel-of-cwd could latch onto the store's own repo"],"finding":"The CODE-ROOT config-read sites (_sync_disabled, tickets_branch, _remote_ref at reads.py:238/:249 and freshness.py:80, _load_scratch at reads.py:374) receive only `tracker` and have no repo_root in scope, so the plan's config.repo_root_or_none() with no explicit arg resolves via REBAR_ROOT > git-toplevel-of-cwd. The plan asserts this is correct but does not establish the load-bearing precondition that these sites run with REBAR_ROOT set (or cwd inside the CODE checkout). If REBAR_ROOT is unset and cwd is the store (or a detached child), and the store is itself a git repo, git-toplevel-of-cwd can resolve the STORE's repo — re-introducing the wrong-root bug via a different path while the guard reports clean.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f22da7dcfa51187cd","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Candidate sites — CODE ROOT list; AC#1","norm_id":"ndd8536cf87390575","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Relocated store, REBAR_ROOT unset, cwd == store dir which is itself a git repo — repo_root_or_none() returns the store's toplevel, not the code checkout","A detached/background reader whose inherited cwd is the store"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference